From fae7d46efe6ccbf0bd0badaa17e608d3cc00afe5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:11:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: a comment names the version of its
 measurement, 1.0 RC5

The comment of the level 3 offsets in the mapping to a display named the
version whose software bridge measured them by its short name alone.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
index fbca7b7..1f86040 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
@@ -1564,7 +1564,7 @@ static void map_to_display(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct dvbridge_hd
      * (PL_HDR_METADATA_CIE_Y: max_pq_y, avg_pq_y; it does not read the minimum) are those of level 1
      * with the offsets of level 3 where the metadata have them and ST 2094-10 6.1.9 allows them
      * (dvbridge_level1_effective()); without level 3 they stay as dvbridge_map_color() set them, so
-     * that such a picture is mapped as before, bit for bit. Measured on the software bridge (RC5): with
+     * that such a picture is mapped as before, bit for bit. Measured on the software bridge (1.0 RC5): with
      * the level 3 offsets of the streams at hand (the averages under the floors of content mapping v2.9,
      * and black shots) BT.2390, spline and SDR give the same bytes; an offset that a colourist sets
      * moves the mapping as it moves level 1. */
-- 
2.53.0

